From: Simone Rota <simone.rota16@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:44:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/19] fix(EDDI): pass the original function as callback to
 non-duplicated functions

A function passed as argument (e.g. the comparator of qsort/bsearch, an
atexit handler) was replaced with its _dup version, that has the duplicated
signature: the non-hardened callee then called it with the original arguments
and the program crashed. The original function is passed when the callee has
no _dup version.
---
 passes/EDDI.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/passes/EDDI.cpp b/passes/EDDI.cpp
index 4c85cea..6f5bebd 100755
--- a/passes/EDDI.cpp
+++ b/passes/EDDI.cpp
@@ -694,6 +694,17 @@ void EDDI::duplicateOperands(
       // operand of the clone instruction
       Function *FnOperand = cast<Function>(V);
       auto DuplicateFn = getFunctionDuplicate(FnOperand);
+      // A function passed as argument to a function without a duplicate (e.g.
+      // the comparator of qsort or a handler registered with atexit) is
+      // called back by non-hardened code with its original signature, so the
+      // original function has to be passed.
+      if (auto *CB = dyn_cast<CallBase>(&I);
+          CB && CB->isArgOperand(&I.getOperandUse(J))) {
+        Function *Callee = CB->getCalledFunction();
+        if (Callee != nullptr && getFunctionDuplicate(Callee) == nullptr) {
+          DuplicateFn = nullptr;
+        }
+      }
       if (DuplicateFn != NULL) {
         I.setOperand(J, DuplicateFn);
         if (IClone != nullptr) {
